iversities and Higher Educational Institutes. These are;\n\n1. Course of study in Performing Arts & Mass Media offered by the Sripalee Campus of the University of Colombo\n\n2. Course of study in Arts offered by the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka\n\n3. Course of study in Communication Studies offered by the Trincomalee Campus of the Eastern University, Sri Lanka\n\n4. Course of study in Peace & Conflict Resolution offered by the University of  Kelaniya\n\n5. Course of study in Islamic Studies offered by the South Eastern University of Sri Lanka\n\n6. Course of study in Arabic Language offered by the South Eastern University of Sri Lanka\n\n7. Course of study in Teaching English as a Second Language (TESL) offered by the University of Kelaniya, University of Sri Jayewardenepura and Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka\n\n8.  Courses of study in Music, Dance, Drama and Theatre and Visual Arts offered by the University of the Visual and Performing Arts\n\n9. Courses of study in Music, Dance and Art & Design offered by the University of Jaffna\n\n10. Courses of study in Music, Dance, Drama & Theatre and Visual & Technological Arts offered by the Swamy Vipulananda Institute of  Aesthetic Studies of the Eastern University, Sri Lanka\n\n<!-- PDF page 43 -->\n\n11. Course of study in Music offered by the University of Sri Jayewardenepura\n\nInformation pertaining to these courses of study is given below.', alternative_group: '', alternative_option: 0, evaluated: false, superseded_by: 'requirement:arts-selection-rules', request_id: 'al-extraction:2.2.1.1:cross-basket-exceptions'}}, {id: 'requirement:al:proposal:2.2.1.1:019:3', props: {id: 'requirement:al:proposal:2.2.1.1:019:3', level: 'A/L', requirement_type: 'al_basket_rule', rule: '{"alternative_group": "", "alternative_option": 0, "common_general_paper": {"condition": "", "minimum_percentage": 0, "required": false}, "conditions": ["- No candidate is allowed to offer three Classical Languages or three Foreign Languages."], "confidence": "high", "eligible_streams": ["Arts"], "evidence_text": "##### Exemptions are;\\n\\n- a. A student can select three National Languages.\\n\\n- e.g: Sinhala, Tamil and English\\n\\n- b. A student can select at least one subject from National Languages and two subjects from Classical Languages.\\n\\n- No candidate is allowed to offer three Classical Languages or three Foreign Languages.\\n\\n- The above guidance is useful to select subject combinations for different degree programmes of a course of study in Arts in almost all Universities and Higher Educational Institutes.\\n\\n- The medium of Instruction of the course of study in Arts offered by the universities are as follows.\\n\\n<!-- Table intentionally left empty; see original PDF page 42 -->\\n\\n- However, some Universities and Higher Educational Institutes offer some degree programmes under Arts Stream which may expect different advanced level subject combinations for selection. The reason for offering such different combinations is to enhance the quality and relevance of such degree programmes for the purpose of employment and to be in line with the expectations of  the society.\\n\\nThere are 11 such courses of study offered by different Universities and Higher Educational Institutes. These are;\\n\\n1. Course of study in Performing Arts & Mass Media offered by the Sripalee Campus of the University of Colombo\\n\\n2. Course of study in Arts offered by the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka\\n\\n3. Course of study in Communication Studies offered by the Trincomalee Campus of the Eastern University, Sri Lanka\\n\\n4. Course of study in Peace & Conflict Resolution offered by the University of  Kelaniya\\n\\n5. Course of study in Islamic Studies offered by the South Eastern University of Sri Lanka\\n\\n6. Course of study in Arabic Language offered by the South Eastern University of Sri Lanka\\n\\n7. Course of study in Teaching English as a Second Language (TESL) offered by the University of Kelaniya, University of Sri Jayewardenepura and Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka\\n\\n8.  Courses of study in Music, Dance, Drama and Theatre and Visual Arts offered by the University of the Visual and Performing Arts\\n\\n9. Courses of study in Music, Dance and Art & Design offered by the University of Jaffna\\n\\n10. Courses of study in Music, Dance, Drama & Theatre and Visual & Technological Arts offered by the Swamy Vipulananda Institute of  Aesthetic Studies of the Eastern University, Sri Lanka\\n\\n<!-- PDF page 43 -->\\n\\n11. Course of study in Music offered by the University of Sri Jayewardenepura\\n\\nInformation pertaining to these courses of study is given below.", "exception_to": "", "minimum_grades": {"grade_condition_text": "", "required_a_grades": 0, "required_b_grades": 0, "required_c_grades": 0, "required_s_grades": 0}, "requirement_type": "al_basket_rule", "review_status": "proposed", "selection_constraints": [{"condition": "- No candidate is allowed to offer three Classical Languages or three Foreign Languages.", "constraint_type": "prohibited_combination", "count": 3, "group_name": "Classical Languages", "subjects": []}, {"condition": "- No candidate is allowed to offer three Classical Languages or three Foreign Languages.", "constraint_type": "prohibited_combination", "count": 3, "group_name": "Foreign Languages", "subjects": []}], "source": {"markdown_line_end": 1508, "markdown_line_start": 1464, "pdf_page": 42, "section": "2.2.1.1"}, "subject_grade_requirements": [], "subject_groups": [], "subjects": [], "target_id": "course:019", "target_type": "Course"}', basis: 'deterministic_parser', extraction_method: 'deterministic', evidence_text: '##### Exemptions are;\n\n- a. A student can select three National Languages.\n\n- e.g: Sinhala, Tamil and English\n\n- b. A student can select at least one subject from National Languages and two subjects from Classical Languages.\n\n- No candidate is allowed to offer three Classical Languages or three Foreign Languages.\n\n- The above guidance is useful to select subject combinations for different degree programmes of a course of study in Arts in almost all Universities and Higher Educational Institutes.\n\n- The medium of Instruction of the course of study in Arts offered by the universities are as follows.\n\n<!-- Table intentionally left empty; see original PDF page 42 -->\n\n- However, some Universities and Higher Educational Institutes offer some degree programmes under Arts Stream which may expect different advanced level subject combinations for selection. The reason for offering such different combinations is to enhance the quality and relevance of such degree programmes for the purpose of employment and to be in line with the expectations of  the society.\n\nThere are 11 such courses of study offered by different Universities and Higher Educational Institutes. These are;\n\n1. Course of study in Performing Arts & Mass Media offered by the Sripalee Campus of the University of Colombo\n\n2. Course of study in Arts offered by the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka\n\n3. Course of study in Communication Studies offered by the Trincomalee Campus of the Eastern University, Sri Lanka\n\n4. Course of study in Peace & Conflict Resolution offered by the University of  Kelaniya\n\n5. Course of study in Islamic Studies offered by the South Eastern University of Sri Lanka\n\n6. Course of study in Arabic Language offered by the South Eastern University of Sri Lanka\n\n7. Course of study in Teaching English as a Second Language (TESL) offered by the University of Kelaniya, University of Sri Jayewardenepura and Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka\n\n8.  Courses of study in Music, Dance, Drama and Theatre and Visual Arts offered by the University of the Visual and Performing Arts\n\n9. Courses of study in Music, Dance and Art & Design offered by the University of Jaffna\n\n10. Courses of study in Music, Dance, Drama & Theatre and Visual & Technological Arts offered by the Swamy Vipulananda Institute of  Aesthetic Studies of the Eastern University, Sri Lanka\n\n<!-- PDF page 43 -->\n\n11. Course of study in Music offered by the University of Sri Jayewardenepura\n\nInformation pertaining to these courses of study is given below.', alternative_group: '', alternative_option: 0, evaluated: false, superseded_by: 'requirement:arts-selection-rules', request_id: 'al-extraction:2.2.1.1:cross-basket-exceptions'}}, {id: 'requirement:al:proposal:2.2.1.1:019:4', props: {id: 'requirement:al:proposal:2.2.1.1:019:4', level: 'A/L', requirement_type: 'al_exception', rule: '{"alternative_group": "", "alternative_option": 0, "common_general_paper": {"condition": "", "minimum_percentage": 0, "required": false}, "conditions": ["2.  Students selecting a combination of  National and Classical languages need not to select any subject from basket 01."], "confidence": "high", "eligible_streams": ["Arts"], "evidence_text": "##### Basket 01- Social Sciences/ Applied Social Studies:\\n\\n1.    Economics\\n\\n2.    Geography\\n\\n3.     History\\n\\n4.   Home Economics\\n\\n5.   Agricultural Science/ Mathematics/ Combined Mathematics\\n\\n6.   Communication & Media Studies\\n\\n7.   Information & Communication Technology\\n\\n8.   Accounting/ Business Statistics\\n\\n9.   Political Science\\n\\n10. Logic & Scientific Method\\n\\n11. One subject from Technological Subjects :\\n\\n- Civil Technology\\n\\n- Electrical, Electronic and Information Technology\\n\\n- Agro Technology\\n\\n- Mechanical Technology\\n\\n- Food Technology\\n\\n- Bio-Resource Technology\\n\\n##### Guidance for selection of subjects from basket 01:\\n\\n- Students should select at least one subject from this basket.\\n\\n- Students can also select all three subjects only from basket 01.\\n\\nThere are three exceptions to this rule. These are;\\n\\n1.  Students selecting three National Languages; Sinhala, Tamil and English from the basket 04 (Language Basket) as the three subjects, need not to select any subject from basket 01.\\n\\n2.  Students selecting a combination of  National and Classical languages need not to select any subject from basket 01.\\n\\n<!-- PDF page 40 -->\\n\\n- **National Languages are;** Sinhala Tamil English\\n\\n- **Classical Languages are;** Arabic Pali Sanskrit\\n\\nFor example, students can select three subjects like Sinhala, Pali and Sanskrit etc. These students need not to select any subject from basket 01.\\n\\nHowever, no candidate can select three classical languages as three subjects. They can select a maximum of two classical languages only.\\n\\n3. Students selecting two languages from the basket 04 and the third subject from Religions and Civilizations or Aesthetic subject classified under basket 02 and 03 given below need not to select any subject from basket 01.", "exception_to": "Basket 01 minimum subject requirement", "minimum_grades": {"grade_condition_text": "", "required_a_grades": 0, "required_b_grades": 0, "required_c_grades": 0, "required_s_grades": 0}, "requirement_type": "al_exception", "review_status": "proposed", "selection_constraints": [{"condition": "2.  Students selecting a combination of  National and Classical languages need not to select any subject from basket 01.", "constraint_type": "allowed_combination", "count": 0, "group_name": "National and Classical Languages", "subjects": []}], "source": {"markdown_line_end": 1338, "markdown_line_start": 1280, "pdf_page": 39, "section": "2.2.1.1"}, "subject_grade_requirements": [], "subject_groups": [], "subjects": [], "target_id": "course:019", "target_type": "Course"}', basis: 'deterministic_parser', extraction_method: 'deterministic', evidence_text: '##### Basket 01- Social Sciences/ Applied Social Studies:\n\n1.    Economics\n\n2.    Geography\n\n3.     History\n\n4.   Home Economics\n\n5.   Agricultural Science/ Mathematics/ Combined Mathematics\n\n6.   Communication & Media Studies\n\n7.   Information & Communication Technology\n\n8.   Accounting/ Business Statistics\n\n9.   Political Science\n\n10. Logic & Scientific Method\n\n11. One subject from Technological Subjects :\n\n- Civil Technology\n\n- Electrical, Electronic and Information Technology\n\n- Agro Technology\n\n- Mechanical Technology\n\n- Food Technology\n\n- Bio-Resource Technology\n\n##### Guidance for selection of subjects from basket 01:\n\n- Students should select at least one subject from this basket.\n\n- Students can also select all three subjects only from basket 01.\n\nThere are three exceptions to this rule. These are;\n\n1.  Students selecting three National Languages; Sinhala, Tamil and English from the basket 04 (Language Basket) as the three subjects, need not to select any subject from basket 01.\n\n2.  Students selecting a combination of  National and Classical languages need not to select any subject from basket 01.\n\n<!-- PDF page 40 -->\n\n- **National Languages are;** Sinhala Tamil English\n\n- **Classical Languages are;** Arabic Pali Sanskrit\n\nFor example, students can select three subjects like Sinhala, Pali and Sanskrit etc. These students need not to select any subject from basket 01.\n\nHowever, no candidate can select three classical languages as three subjects. They can select a maximum of two classical languages only.\n\n3. Students selecting two languages from the basket 04 and the third subject from Religions and Civilizations or Aesthetic subject classified under basket 02 and 03 given below need not to select any subject from basket 01.', alternative_group: '', alternative_option: 0, evaluated: false, superseded_by: 'requirement:arts-selection-rules', request_id: 'al-extraction:2.2.1.1:basket-1'}}, {id: 'requirement:al:proposal:2.2.1.1:019:5', props: {id: 'requirement:al:proposal:2.2.1.1:019:5', level: 'A/L', requirement_type: 'al_basket_rule', rule: '{"alternative_group": "", "alternative_option": 0, "common_general_paper": {"condition": "", "minimum_percentage": 0, "required": false}, "conditions": ["However, no candidate can select three classical languages as three subjects. They can select a maximum of two classical languages only."], "confidence": "high", "eligible_streams": ["Arts"], "evidence_text": "##### Basket 01- Social Sciences/ Applied Social Studies:\\n\\n1.    Economics\\n\\n2.    Geography\\n\\n3.     History\\n\\n4.   Home Economics\\n\\n5.   Agricultural Science/ Mathematics/ Combined Mathematics\\n\\n6.   Communication & Media Studies\\n\\n7.   Information & Communication Technology\\n\\n8.   Accounting/ Business Statistics\\n\\n9.   Political Science\\n\\n10. Logic & Scientific Method\\n\\n11. One subject from Technological Subjects :\\n\\n- Civil Technology\\n\\n- Electrical, Electronic and Information Technology\\n\\n- Agro Technology\\n\\n- Mechanical Technology\\n\\n- Food Technology\\n\\n- Bio-Resource Technology\\n\\n##### Guidance for selection of subjects from basket 01:\\n\\n- Students should select at least one subject from this basket.\\n\\n- Students can also select all three subjects only from basket 01.\\n\\nThere are three exceptions to this rule. These are;\\n\\n1.  Students selecting three National Languages; Sinhala, Tamil and English from the basket 04 (Language Basket) as the three subjects, need not to select any subject from basket 01.\\n\\n2.  Students selecting a combination of  National and Classical languages need not to select any subject from basket 01.\\n\\n<!-- PDF page 40 -->\\n\\n- **National Languages are;** Sinhala Tamil English\\n\\n- **Classical Languages are;** Arabic Pali Sanskrit\\n\\nFor example, students can select three subjects like Sinhala, Pali and Sanskrit etc. These students need not to select any subject from basket 01.\\n\\nHowever, no candidate can select three classical languages as three subjects. They can select a maximum of two classical languages only.\\n\\n3. Students selecting two languages from the basket 04 and the third subject from Religions and Civilizations or Aesthetic subject classifi